.TH GETTICKET.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
GetTicket.sh \- kinit from a keytab for a principal hard\-coded in the script (deprecated; configured for DUNE)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bin/GetTicket.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Deprecated.
For Mu2e service identities use
.B get\-kerberos\-ticket
.I identity
from
.BR mu2edaq\-kerberos ;
for a personal ticket,
.BR kinit (1).
.PP
The script runs one keytab
.B kinit
for the principal and keytab set in its first lines.
As shipped those are a
.B DUNE
control\-room identity, not a Mu2e one:
.PP
.EX
pname="dune\-controlroom\-fnal/dune/dune\-cr\-01@FNAL.GOV"
keytab="dune\-controlroom\-fnal.keytab"
keytabpath="$HOME/.krb5"
.EE
.PP
When
.B TERM_PROGRAM
is
.B Apple_Terminal
it runs
.BR "kinit \-f \-A \-k \-t" ;
in any other terminal, including iTerm2 and the VS Code terminal on
macOS, it runs the MIT form
.BR "kinit \-5 \-F \-A \-k \-t" ,
whose
.B \-F
means "not forwardable" to Heimdal.
.B kinit
output is discarded.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.I $HOME/.krb5/dune\-controlroom\-fnal.keytab
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B TERM_PROGRAM
selects the
.B kinit
flags as above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.BR kinit 's
status.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
bash bin/GetTicket.sh && klist
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR get\-kerberos\-ticket (1),
.BR kinit (1),
.BR mu2e\-krb\-cron.py (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
